        "id": "p10-q8-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Differentiate $y=e^{\\sin x}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y'=\\cos x\\,e^{\\sin x}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y'&=e^{\\sin x}\\cos x\\\\y'&=\\cos x\\,e^{\\sin x}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 13
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q8-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Hence find, in the domain $0\\le x\\le 2\\pi$, the $x$-coordinates of the points on the curve $y=e^{\\sin x}$ where the tangent is horizontal.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2},\\dfrac{3\\pi}{2}$",
          "worked": "For a horizontal tangent, $y'=0$.\n\n$$\\cos x\\,e^{\\sin x}=0$$\n\nSince $e^{\\sin x}>0$, we need $\\cos x=0$. In $[0,2\\pi]$,\n\n$$x=\\frac{\\pi}{2},\\frac{3\\pi}{2}.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      }
    ]
  },
